  "question": {
    "text": "A sphere is rotating between two rough inclined walls as shown in figure. Coefficient of friction between each wall and the sphere is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> be the frictional forces at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0026_842afe94ba2b.jpg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 136px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <msqrt> <mn>3</mn> </msqrt> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <msqrt> <mn>3</mn> </msqrt> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>+</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>+</mo> <msqrt><mn>3</mn> </msqrt></mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mo>+</mo> <mn>2</mn> <msqrt> <mn>3</mn> </msqrt> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μ</mi></math> be the friction coefficient between sphere and each wall. Free body diagram of sphere is<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0026_72b425f04105.jpg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 133px;\" /><br /><br />Net force on the sphere in horizontal diarection is zero.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>cos</mi><msup><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ο</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>cos</mi><msup><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ο</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>cos</mi><msup><mn>30</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ο</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>cos</mi><msup><mn>30</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ο</mi></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br />Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> we get,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>⇒</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>"
  }
